  # Benchmarking AI Agent Memory: Is a Filesystem All You Need?
## Memory for AI Agents
[MemGPT](https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.08560) introduced [memory management for agents](https://www.letta.com/blog/agent-memory/) by creating a memory hierarchy inspired by a traditional operating system (OS). Many agentic systems today, including Letta, implement MemGPT’s design to enable long-term memory in LLM agents.

## Attempts at Benchmarking Memory Tools (e.g., Mem0, LangMem, Zep)
One memory tool creator, Mem0, published [controversial results](https://www.reddit.com/r/LangChain/comments/1kash7b/i_benchmarked_openai_memory_vs_langmem_vs_letta/) claiming to have run MemGPT on LoCoMo. Mem0 [did not respond](https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0/issues/3004) to requests for clarification on how the benchmarking numbers were computed, or provide any modified MemGPT implementation that supports meaningful backfill of LoCoMo data.

