## Zep: A Temporal Knowledge Graph Architecture for Agent Memory
31Likes

Jun 42026

Zep: A Temporal Knowledge Graph Architecture for Agent Memory

Unlike traditional systems that rely on static corpora, Zep integrates a temporally-aware knowledge graph engine, Graphiti, to dynamically synthesize unstructured conversational data and structured business data while maintaining historical relationships. Zep’s hierarchical knowledge graph structure mirrors human memory, consisting of episodic, semantic, and community subgraphs that store raw data, extracted entities, and high-level domain summaries, respectively.

In the Deep Memory Retrieval (DMR) task, Zep achieved a 94.8% accuracy, outperforming MemGPT (93.4%). On the more demanding LongMemEval benchmark, Zep achieved up to an 18.5% accuracy improvement and reduced latency by 90%, excelling in complex tasks like temporal reasoning and multi-session information synthesis.

Zep’s innovations include a bi-temporal model for accurate historical tracking, efficient retrieval through multi-method search and reranking, and scalable, latency-optimized performance.

